host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan molts child to dependent -- the word the arc had already earned
prompt Seat a breach molt deep debride of Caravan's use of child in favour of dependent, and children in favour of dependents; approve a force push; molt every link the Caravan README references and every code file it reaches, down to the leaves; molt the imported Caravan and Tally code files too and make them relevant to the latest Caravan and Tally development state
think Cairn before anything moved. A deep debride force-pushes both remotes, so the walk-back nib is unreachable there afterwards -- recorded 5f6ec40c39 in crux/CAIRNS.md and named plainly that it survives on this pier alone, on the branch pre-dependent-debride-20260819. A cairn that claims a walk-back the remotes will not hold would be worse than none.
think Measured the target before touching it rather than trusting the grep that found 93 files. Enumerated every distinct token carrying the word: 2,067 bare child, 375 children, and the identifier family around them -- ChildSlot, ChildId, InvalidChild, ChildNeverExited, max_children, max_caps_per_child, max_peers_per_child, max_restarts_per_child, run_child, find_child, add_child, child_count, child_of, no_such_child.
think One elder must stay, and finding it was the load-bearing check: std.process.Child appears 7 times across cohort.rye, concurrent.rye, and subscribe_poll_service.rye. That is Zig's name at an inherited seam, and inherited-names policy says we do not rename what we did not name. The molt protects it by placeholder before every other substitution and restores it after.
think Word boundaries were the second trap. A naive \b pattern misses per_child entirely, since underscore is a word character -- the first pass skipped refusal_reason_test.rye for exactly that reason and a second sweep caught it. Enumerating the camel tokens first (Children before Child) and then replacing on plain substring, having already protected the one seam, is both simpler and provably complete: the residual grep is empty but for std.process.Child.
think Checked for a collision before choosing the word. Caravan already uses depend, depends, and dependency in prose 15 times, and none of them is an identifier -- so dependent collides with nothing mechanical. Two prose lines would have read the components its running dependents depend on, and those were hand-corrected to rely on rather than left awkward.
think The leaves were the real work, and the witnesses found them rather than reasoning finding them. Forty-eight of 52 rungs went GREEN on the first run and the four REDs were exactly the Glow desks: the pedestal shapes src/lib/shape-caravan-max-children.glow and shape-caravan-max-caps-per-child.glow, the wall gate-caravan-children-bound-u32.glow, and the tend limb witnesses that grep them by name. Renamed all three and their content, and the four rungs came home.
think The deepest leaf was the one no witness caught, because its witness was already RED for another reason. glow/lower_bartis.rye lowers the Glow arms caps_lawful and children_lawful into generated Zig that reads caravan.max_caps_per_child and caravan.max_children through a directory alias -- constants this molt had just renamed. Left alone it would have been a silent break waiting for the next Glow lap. Repaired the lowering, molted the arm to dependents_lawful, and renamed both glow/gen desks that call it.
think That supposed pre-existing RED turned out to be a stale glow/.cache: once the cache regenerated with the new caravan alias, glow_compose_tend_unary_witness came home GREEN with 345: Caravan kin -- caps at 8 and 9, dependents at 4 and 5 in its own voice. Worth naming, because a red that heals on a rebuild is a cache fact rather than a code fact, and calling it the wrong one would have booked an allocation against nothing.
think Tally needed no molt, and proving that was the honest answer rather than a skipped step. Its two symlinked marks carry no child at all; tally/gardens.rye uses child for a sub-region of a memory arena, which is a different meaning that dependent would misdescribe; and tally/no_padding.rye's info.child is Zig's own type-info field. The caller map still names caravan reaching tally_copy and parse_int, which is exactly what the symlinks are, so the map is current and tally_caller_map_witness proves it GREEN.
think Left dated testimony standing. Counsel, waymarks, dated active-designing, and 2,000-odd session logs keep every child they ever wrote -- they are records of what was true when written, and the debride's own rule is a named target rather than a sweep. What moved is living code and living cards: caravan, its witnesses, the Glow desks and lowering, mand/capabilities.rye, the manual page, src/lib/README.md, linengrow's citation, crux/REMEMBER.md, and context/LEXICON.md.
obs Three witnesses went RED together mid-round -- limb1, limb2, limb3 -- and re-ran GREEN twice immediately after with nothing changed between. The cause was contention: two witness runs at once, both writing glow/.cache and caravan/bin. That is a real shared-state fragility in the witness surface worth naming, and it is why the final verification sweep runs strictly single-threaded.
obs A grep-shaped rename would have been finished in one command and wrong in four places. Every genuine leaf -- the Glow pedestals, the wall gate, the lowered constants, the linengrow citation -- was found by running something rather than by reading something. Measurement beat memory here in the plainest possible way.
obs The word is better than the one it replaces, and the arc had already earned it. By unhand.rye a supervised process is weighed by the line it holds rather than by the ceiling its domain was granted; by confer.rye and revoke.rye its reach travels to it and returns from it while it runs. Something held up by what it was granted is a dependent. Offspring was never what the rings were describing.
obs REMEMBER's JARL lines keep their own child, correctly: a Kumara point re-parenting to a new sponsor is a different domain with a genuine parent-offspring reading. Molting those would have been the vocabulary sweep overreaching past its target.
loom witness=caravan_suite_witness result=GREEN rungs=52 bijection=whole
loom molt files_working_tree=97 bare_child=2067 children=375 seams_kept=7 renames=6
loom history blobs_targeted=638 blobs_scanned_clean=285 commits_rewritten=3090 commits_resigned=3090 caravan_commits=51
file caravan/README.md the ladder molted whole, the header restamped, and a vocabulary note seating why dependent is the honest word and why std.process.Child stays
file caravan/capabilities.rye max_dependents, max_caps_per_dependent, DependentSlot -- the table every other ring derives from
file tools/caravan_dependents_a1_gate_bound_witness.rish the one witness whose filename carried the word, renamed with its roster line and its suite registration
file src/lib/shape-caravan-max-dependents.glow the Glow pedestal naming the bound beside the Rye that owns it, renamed with its sibling shape and wall gate
file glow/lower_bartis.rye the deepest leaf -- the lowering that reads caravan's constants into generated Zig, repaired in the same round that renamed them
file mand/capabilities.rye Caravan's capability table as Mand carries it, molted to match its elder
file manual/reference/caravan-capabilities.md the reader-facing page, molted so the manual and the module say the same words
file context/LEXICON.md Dependent seated as vocabulary, naming what moved, what stayed, and why
file crux/CAIRNS.md the walk-back marker recorded before anything moved, honest that the nib is local-only after the force push
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live edge lines molted; the JARL sponsor lines left alone, since that child is a different word
recommend keep-going the working-tree molt is GREEN on metal across all 52 Caravan rungs, the Glow tend and compose families, the a1 gate suites, Tally's caller map, TAME style, and the ASCII card guard -- so the approved deep debride runs in this same round: 638 Caravan blobs rewritten across 3,090 commits, the six path renames carried through history, the caravan: commit subjects molted, every commit re-signed, and a force push to origin and xykj61. The one honest cost is named rather than softened -- every downstream clone must re-clone, and the walk-back nib 5f6ec40c39 lives only on this pier afterwards. one_clock_witness stands RED for a reason this round did not cause and did not fix: the pier's host zone reads UTC rather than America/New_York by name, so every stamp here is taken with an explicit TZ. That is worth a red of its own, on Keaton's word.
